  "body": "## What changed\n\n`crates/app/src/rest.rs` had grown to 424 lines, past AGENTS.md's ~400-line limit. The code that walks the operations ahead of a consumer (`Ahead`, `path_hash`, `ahead_of`, `digest_of`, lines 73–253) moves without changes into a new submodule, `crates/app/src/rest/ahead.rs`, visible only to its parent (`pub(super)`). `rest.rs` keeps the module's laws, `PriorState`, `PriorPlan` and the public API (`prior_digest`, `prior_state`, `prior_plan`, `prior_stale`) with the same signatures. Two intra-doc links now point at `super::`. The new file has its own provenance header.\n\n- `rest.rs`: 424 → 245 lines\n- `rest/ahead.rs`: 193 lines\n\nNo behaviour change: no function bodies were edited, and the hash seeds and field order are the same, so every stamp digests exactly as before.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The suites #127 names all pass unchanged: `drill_prior` (10), `drill_prior_kinds` (4), `vertical_rapid_stock` (4), `remachining` (6).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets`: clean.\n- `cargo fmt --check`: the two touched files are clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (app suites): everything passes except two tests that **also fail on `upstream/main` without this change**, so they already exist upstream and this PR doesn't affect them:\n  - `drilling_cross_box::a_cylinder_stock_chain_is_unchanged_bit_for_bit`: \"the round-bar chains moved\"\n  - `drilling_cross_spindle::a_cross_drill_off_the_world_origin_under_a_moved_g54_drills_the_on_origin_chain`: \"lathe: the same chain, move for move\"\n\n  These look connected to the recent cross-hole entry fixes (9a095b7, 3b974ea). I found no open issue for them.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNone new: this is a refactor, and it is pinned by the existing suites above. The `#[test]` count is unchanged; `rest.rs` had no inline tests.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #127\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
